{"id": "idaho-1", "headline": "Idaho seniors lose Medicare Advantage plans", "source": "Idaho Capital Sun", "url": "https://idahocapitalsun.com/2026/11/26/health-insurers-are-dropping-idaho-medicare-advantage-plans-that-cover-tens-of-thousands/", "published": "2026-11-26", "url_verified": true, "pages": ["More than 60,000 Idahoans are enrolled in Medicare Advantage plans that will be canceled statewide or in their county next year, according to federal data analyzed by Idaho insurance brokers. That is nearly a third of Idaho seniors with private Medicare coverage. Medicare open enrollment ends Dec. 7. Brokers urge seniors to read mailed notices and seek help, saying the cancellations are causing panic. Some people in North Idaho and rural areas may not find comparable plans. Idaho Department of Insurance Director Dean Cameron pointed to free help from licensed agents or the state's SHIBA counselors.", "Those whose plans end may be able to switch to another plan or traditional Medicare through a special enrollment period. A broker said insurers have not seen federal pay rates keep up with inflation. Source: Idaho Capital Sun."], "qr": {"n": 41, "rows": ["11111110100110000101100110100011101111111", "10000010001000001010111100101010101000001", "10111010101101000010100111110001101011101", "10111010111011110101001011100100101011101", "10111010100001011101011010111101001011101", "10000010001111101101110010001001001000001", "11111110101010101010101010101010101111111", "00000000001100011110001000101110000000000", "11110010100110111110010010011111110011101", "01010100101000001001110111100011111111011", "10011010001101100010011101001100001100110", "00010100100101111001001101000011011100001", "01001010100111010111001011100101000001100", "00111101110110111101110010011001001000111", "01010111100101100011101011001011101000011", "00111000101100010001010000010010000111010", "10010010101001001010111011100010110110010", "11001000110110110110101101110110100101000", "101010101110111110